# A word that beats: a strong swell and a smaller one per beat, then rest
law heartbeat
kind motion
claim each beat swells the glyphs twice: a strong swell centred at 10% of the beat and a swell 0.6 as strong at 30%, then the glyphs rest
claim the rate is bpm beats a minute, the strong swell grows the glyphs by depth of their size, each glyph runs 40 ms behind the one before it
param bpm number = 72 range 40 180
param depth number = 0.06 range 0 0.2
period 60000 / bpm
stagger 40
let first = max(0, 1 - ((phase - 0.10) / 0.08) ^ 2)
let second = max(0, 1 - ((phase - 0.30) / 0.07) ^ 2)
let swell = max(first, 0.6 * second)
channel scale = 1 + depth * swell
channel luminance = 0.9 + 0.1 * swell
